Rule 1 (input tensor must have at least 2 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must have a boolean, integer, float, or complex data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 4 (the last two dimensions of the input tensor must have positive sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) > 0 else false
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor must have a dimension between 2 and 6)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ 6
>>
Rule 6 (tensor must have a floating-point or complex data type: 6–10)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 7 (the input tensor should be 2-dimensional or 3-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 3
>>
Rule 8 (for a 2D input matrix, both dimensions must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0
